@.str.66 = private unnamed_addr constant [3971 x i8] c"usage: pbrt [<options>] <filename.pbrt...>\0A\0ARendering options:\0A  --cropwindow <x0,x1,y0,y1>    Specify an image crop window w.r.t. [0,1]^2.\0A  --debugstart <values>         Inform the Integrator where to start rendering for\0A                                faster debugging. (<values> are Integrator-specific\0A                                and come from error message text.)\0A  --disable-image-textures      Always return the average value of image textures.\0A  --disable-pixel-jitter        Always sample pixels at their centers.\0A  --disable-texture-filtering   Point-sample all textures.\0A  --disable-wavelength-jitter   Always sample the same %d wavelengths of light.\0A  --displacement-edge-scale <s> Scale target triangle edge length by given value.\0A                                (Default: 1)\0A  --display-server <addr:port>  Connect to display server at given address and port\0A                                to display the image as it's being rendered.\0A  --force-diffuse               Convert all materials to be diffuse.)\0A  --fullscreen                  Render fullscreen. Only supported with --interactive.\0A  --help                        Print this help text.\0A  --interactive                 Enable interactive rendering mode.\0A  --mse-reference-image         Filename for reference image to use for MSE computation.\0A  --mse-reference-out           File to write MSE error vs spp results.\0A  --nthreads <num>              Use specified number of threads for rendering.\0A  --outfile <filename>          Write the final image to the given filename.\0A  --pixel <x,y>                 Render just the specified pixel.\0A  --pixelbounds <x0,x1,y0,y1>   Specify an image crop window w.r.t. pixel coordinates.\0A  --pixelmaterial <x,y>         Print information about the material visible in the\0A                                center of the pixel's extent.\0A  --pixelstats                  Record per-pixel statistics and write additional images\0A                                with their values.\0A  --quick                       Automatically reduce a number of quality settings\0A                                to render more quickly.\0A  --quiet                       Suppress all text output other than error messages.\0A  --render-coord-sys <name>     Coordinate system to use for the scene when rendering,\0A                                where name is \22camera\22, \22cameraworld\22, or \22world\22.\0A  --seed <n>                    Set random number generator seed. Default: 0.\0A  --stats                       Print various statistics after rendering completes.\0A  --spp <n>                     Override number of pixel samples specified in scene\0A                                description file.\0A  --wavefront                   Use wavefront volumetric path integrator.\0A  --write-partial-images        Periodically write the current image to disk, rather\0A                                than waiting for the end of rendering. Default: disabled.\0A\0ALogging options:\0A  --log-file <filename>         Filename to write logging messages to. Default: none;\0A                                messages are printed to standard error. Implies\0A                                --log-level verbose if specified.\0A  --log-level <level>           Log messages at or above this level, where <level>\0A                                is \22verbose\22, \22error\22, or \22fatal\22. Default: \22error\22.\0A  --log-utilization             Periodically print processor and memory use in verbose-\0A                                level logging.\0A\0AReformatting options:\0A  --format                      Print a reformatted version of the input file(s) to\0A                                standard output. Does not render an image.\0A  --toply                       Print a reformatted version of the input file(s) to\0A                                standard output and convert all triangle meshes to\0A                                PLY files. Does not render an image.\0A  --upgrade                     Upgrade a pbrt-v3 file to pbrt-v4's format.\0A\00", align 1
